WEBVTT

00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:04.532
When we find missing values, the first step is to measure the problem.

00:00:04.532 --> 00:00:08.562
A count tells us how many values are missing in each column.

00:00:08.562 --> 00:00:14.292
A percentage tells us how large that problem is relative to the size of the dataset.

00:00:14.292 --> 00:00:20.777
One missing value in a ten-row dataset means ten percent of the data in that column is missing.

00:00:20.777 --> 00:00:25.452
One missing value in a million-row dataset is usually much less important.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.432
Run the code and look at both the count and percentage.

00:00:29.432 --> 00:00:37.472
Notice that the code creates a small missingness report and sorts the columns so the most incomplete columns appear

00:00:37.472 --> 00:00:44.132
first. This pattern is useful in real projects because it gives you a quick overview of data completeness.

00:00:44.132 --> 00:00:47.662
Do not decide what to do with missing values yet.

00:00:47.662 --> 00:00:53.219
The goal here is only to understand where they are and how serious the problem may be.
